
# This is the .gitignore for my ~/.config ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME) folder
# It is NOT a global configuration file, despite living in the folder where global configuration files live.
# It *governs* the ignore rules that git will follow when enforcing version control upon those files.
# Therefore, it needs to 1) be in this folder, and 2) have this exact name. Otherwise,
# it won't work.

# Style-wise, I'd like this file to contain folders that represent large swaths of files that need to be ignored
# The sort of things that should otherwise live in a different place, like $XDG_DATA_HOME or $XDG_CACHE_HOME

aws/*/cache/
docker/buildx/
eksctl/clusters/
maven/mvnd/registry/
maven/wrapper/dists/
vcsh/repo.d/

# These specific files are of the sort listed above, but not swaths.
# These are UI files that generally control the layout etc. of a UI.
# They can change whenever the ui changes. Let's not track that
btop/btop.conf
git/gitk
# There's some stuff in gitk which tries to ignore the argo_manifest branch
# set permviews {{{All Branches & Tags} {} {--all --branches --tags --remotes} {}}
# {{Command line} {} {--all ^argo_manifests --exclude=*argo_manifests} {}}
htop/htoprc
neofetch/config.conf
mc/ini
mc/panels.ini
